## How this file works

The developer and the agent keep this list together:
- The developer adds features to "To do".
- The agent builds them in order, opens one PR (or ships one version) per feature, then moves the feature to "Done" with a changelog.
- Unless a task asks for a human check, the agent may run the whole flow and commit on its own.
- Either side can file an issue and mark it fixed or open. The agent fixes open issues in the next version.
- Clean up "Done" and fixed issues now and then: keep the last 5 versions, drop older ones that are more than 7 days old.

